## Foundry Plugin — Integration Test Environment
## Copy to .env.test and fill in values before running integration tests.
## .env.test is gitignored — never commit real credentials.

## ⛔ HOST PATHS — REQUIRED. docker-compose.yml interpolates both with NO default,
## so leaving them unset fails the stack with a bare "variable is not set" that
## names neither this file nor what it wanted. They were referenced only by the
## compose file and documented NOWHERE until 2026-08-15, which made the harness
## un-setup-able from its own example.
##
## FOUNDRY_CACHE_DIR — a dir holding a pre-downloaded foundryvtt-<version>.zip
##   matching FOUNDRY_VERSION below. felddy then installs from cache and skips
##   the download/auth entirely. Mounted READ-WRITE: felddy v14 writes its own
##   housekeeping (CACHEDIR.TAG, backoff_state.json) even when reusing the zip,
##   so a read-only mount makes it bail.
##   With no cached zip it downloads, which needs valid USERNAME/PASSWORD below.
## FOUNDRY_SYSTEMS_DIR — a dir containing the game systems (dnd5e, and optionally
##   cyphersystem). The WHOLE systems dir is mounted, not a subdir, so Docker
##   does not create a root-owned parent that felddy (uid 1000) then cannot
##   manage — that shows up as EACCES on its README scan.
FOUNDRY_CACHE_DIR=
FOUNDRY_SYSTEMS_DIR=

## (Optional) Foundry APP version the harness runs. Defaults to 14.361 in
## docker-compose.yml, which is DELIBERATE and not drift: it is the version
## module.json declares `compatibility.verified`, the version the fixture world
## pins as coreVersion/minimum, and the version a dozen "MEASURED live (v14.361)"
## comments in module/scripts/ record Foundry's behaviour at. Changing it is a
## compatibility bump that needs those probes re-run — not a version bump.
## Your FOUNDRY_CACHE_DIR should hold the zip for whatever this resolves to.
# FOUNDRY_VERSION=14.361

## FoundryVTT credentials (felddy/foundryvtt image)
FOUNDRY_LICENSE_KEY=
FOUNDRY_USERNAME=
FOUNDRY_PASSWORD=
FOUNDRY_ADMIN_KEY=cfgtestadmin

## Core platform — local dev stack (npm run dev)
## Use http://localhost:10001 when testing against the local dev stack,
## or a staging URL when testing against staging.
CORE_API_URL=http://localhost:10001

## Test campaign — must exist in the Core environment above.
## If blank, globalSetup will create one automatically (requires CORE_ADMIN_API_KEY).
CORE_TEST_CAMPAIGN_ID=

## CFG API key for self-hosted integration tests.
## Generate at: core.crit-fumble.com → Account → API Keys
## The key must have access to CORE_TEST_CAMPAIGN_ID.
CORE_TEST_API_KEY=

## (Optional) Admin API key used by globalSetup to create a test campaign.
## Only needed if CORE_TEST_CAMPAIGN_ID is blank.
CORE_ADMIN_API_KEY=
